ide Champagne."]],"style":{"notes":["Most Bordeaux is red, with sweet and dry whites, rosé and sparkling Crémant de Bordeaux making up the rest.","Plain Bordeaux AOC wines are fruity, with little oak, and are made to drink young.","Left Bank reds lean on Cabernet Sauvignon and are concentrated, tannic and long lived.","Right Bank reds lean on Merlot and often have great fruit concentration and softer tannins.","Graves is best known for dry whites, and Sauternes for some of the world's most famous sweet wines."],"of":"Bordeaux"},"blurb":{"text":"A sparkling wine appellation. It is made from the Bordeaux grapes, red and white, including Merlot, Cabernet Sauvignon, Sémillon and Sauvignon."},"study":true,"sources":[{"name":"Candiago et al. 2022, A geospatial inventory of regulatory information for wine protected designations of origin in Europe, Scientific Data (product specifications as of 2021)","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-022-01513-0"},{"name":"INAO, the appellation's cahier des charges, chapter V (grapes and their shares), from the Bulletin officiel du ministère de l'Agriculture (Licence Ouverte)","url":"https://www.inao.gouv.fr/rechercher-un-produit"},{"name":"Fick and Hijmans 2017, WorldClim 2.1 monthly averages for 1970 to 2000, 2.5 minute grid (about 4.5 km)","url":"https://www.worldclim.org/data/worldclim21.html"},{"name":"Beck et al. 2023, High-resolution (1 km) Koppen-Geiger maps, Scientific Data (1991 to 2020)","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-023-02549-6"},{"name":"Winkler, Cook, Kliewer and Lider 1974, General Viticulture, University of California Press (heat summation regions)","url":null},{"name":"Jones 2010, Climate, grapes, and wine: structure and suitability in a variable and changing climate, VIII International Terroir Congress (which grapes suit which growing season temperatures)","url":"https://ives-openscience.eu/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Climate_Grape_Wine_Jones.pdf"},{"name":"Wikipedia, Appellation d'origine contrôlée (what the l